From f82f001e034c4f5e3f7ce5cea6607c7fd3e867b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Price <thesamprice@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 15:09:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] mdns: fix probing on single-stack netifs in dual-stack builds

When LWIP_IPV4 and LWIP_IPV6 are both enabled,
mdns_probe_and_announce() only counts a probe when sending on both
address families succeeds.

This causes probing to never complete when a netif has an address for
only one family.  For an IPv4-only netif, the IPv6 probe is attempted
despite there being no valid IPv6 address, and its failure prevents
sent_num from advancing.  Conversely, an IPv6-only netif does not reach
the IPv6 probe at all, because the IPv4 condition guards the enclosing
block.

Only attempt a probe for an address family when the netif has a valid
address for that family.  Count the probe when all applicable sends
succeed and at least one address family was probed.

The IPv6 availability test uses
ip6_addr_isvalid(netif_ip6_addr_state(netif, i)), which is what this
module already uses when deciding which IPv6 addresses produce records.

Observed on an IPv4-only netif with LWIP_IPV4=1 and LWIP_IPV6=1: without
this change, 299 probe packets were captured in 12.6 seconds with no
announcement.  With this change the responder sends three probes
followed by two announcements and completes, as RFC 6762 sections 8.1
and 8.3 describe.
---

Notes for the list, not part of the commit message:

* No regression test accompanies this.  test/unit/mdns/test_mdns.c today
  covers name parsing and building only -- readname_*, add_label_*,
  domain_eq_* -- and has no netif, no capturing linkoutput and nothing
  that drives mdns_probe_and_announce() or sys_check_timeouts().  Testing
  the four interesting configurations

      v4+v6 build, IPv4-only netif   -> probing completes
      v4+v6 build, IPv6-only netif   -> probing completes
      v4+v6 build, both configured   -> both probed, completes
      v4+v6 build, neither           -> waits, does not count a probe

  therefore needs scaffolding added to that file rather than a case added
  to an existing fixture.  I am happy to write it if you would like the
  fix and the test together -- say so and I will send a v2.

* How this was found and verified: an lwIP 2.2 build with LWIP_IPV4=1 and
  LWIP_IPV6=1 on an interface holding only an IPv4 address, observed from
  a packet capture of the interface rather than from inside the
  application.  Before: 299 probes in 12.6 s, no announcement, and the
  responder never leaves MDNS_STATE_PROBE_WAIT.  After: three probes at
  the usual spacing, then two announcements, then quiet.

* The IPv6-only half of the defect is by inspection rather than by
  measurement.  I have run the IPv4-only case; the IPv6-only case follows
  from the same control flow -- the outer LWIP_IPV4 condition guards the
  block containing the IPv6 probe -- but I have not exercised it.
 src/apps/mdns/mdns.c | 37 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 28 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/apps/mdns/mdns.c b/src/apps/mdns/mdns.c
index b3ca2f3..ef43846 100644
--- a/src/apps/mdns/mdns.c
+++ b/src/apps/mdns/mdns.c
@@ -2298,20 +2298,39 @@ mdns_probe_and_announce(void* arg)
     case MDNS_STATE_OFF:
     case MDNS_STATE_PROBE_WAIT:
     case MDNS_STATE_PROBING:
+    {
+      int probe_ok = 1;
+      int probe_sent = 0;
+
 #if LWIP_IPV4
-      /*if ipv4 wait with probing until address is set*/
-      if (!ip4_addr_isany_val(*netif_ip4_addr(netif)) &&
-          mdns_send_probe(netif, &v4group) == ERR_OK)
+      if (!ip4_addr_isany_val(*netif_ip4_addr(netif))) {
+        probe_sent = 1;
+        if (mdns_send_probe(netif, &v4group) != ERR_OK) {
+          probe_ok = 0;
+        }
+      }
 #endif
-      {
+
 #if LWIP_IPV6
-        if (mdns_send_probe(netif, &v6group) == ERR_OK)
-#endif
-        {
-          mdns->state = MDNS_STATE_PROBING;
-          mdns->sent_num++;
+      {
+        int i;
+        for (i = 0; i < LWIP_IPV6_NUM_ADDRESSES; i++) {
+          if (ip6_addr_isvalid(netif_ip6_addr_state(netif, i))) {
+            probe_sent = 1;
+            if (mdns_send_probe(netif, &v6group) != ERR_OK) {
+              probe_ok = 0;
+            }
+            break;
+          }
         }
       }
+#endif
+
+      if (probe_sent && probe_ok) {
+        mdns->state = MDNS_STATE_PROBING;
+        mdns->sent_num++;
+      }
+    }
 
       if (mdns->sent_num >= MDNS_PROBE_COUNT) {
         mdns->state = MDNS_STATE_ANNOUNCE_WAIT;
-- 
